  "recipe": {
    "alignment": "Source symbol -> axis gene_index by precedence: canonical axis symbol; gene_crosswalk.csv alias/previous rows; pinned HGNC alias_symbol / prev_symbol; Ensembl id (version stripped) via the axis ensembl_id or the HGNC ensembl_gene_id. Multi-candidate aliases are ambiguous and unresolved, never guessed; unresolved symbols are counted and reported.",
    "deg": "Continuous per-contrast effect score |log2FC| * -log10(padj) with padj floored at 1e-300; NA padj (DESeq2 independent filtering) is treated as non-significant with score 0, not dropped from the measured set. A gene scores the maximum over its source contrasts (declared collapse rule); direction and padj come from that winning contrast and n_contrasts_supporting counts padj < 0.05 contrasts.",
    "direction": "Per gene the significant DEG contrast with the largest effect score across all DEG sources gives the direction; exact ties break by the declared source order and are counted. The symmetric rule counts genes equally, the abs_log2fc rule weights each gene by its winning |log2FC|.",
    "expression_collapse": "Duplicate source symbols resolving to one axis gene are averaged on the deposited log expression.",
    "fusion": "Unweighted sum of rank_norm = rank / n_measured (unmeasured = 1.0) over the fused sources; primary fused rank is ascending rank_sum with gene_index tie-break. rank_sum_animal_half re-weights the two animal MIRI sources at 0.5 (reported sensitivity, not chosen); the primary fusion is unweighted.",
    "hvg": "Seurat-style normalized dispersion on the item's deposited log expression: per-gene mean over finite samples, sample variance / mean, log dispersion standardized in 20 equal-width log1p-mean bins, singleton bins score 1, undefined dispersion sorts last, gene_index tie-break. Same family as output/api/bases/hvg.py; deliberate difference: no expm1 recovery because the disease matrices are heterogeneous non-invertible log scales, so the statistics are computed on the deposited log values directly.",
    "inflection": "Kneedle online S=1.0 (first interior local maximum of the normalized arc y_norm - x_norm) plus the second-difference peak; accepted only when both candidates agree within 25% and the knee exceeds 0.01 normalized units, otherwise an explicit \"inflection\": false.",
    "overlap": "TenV HVG sets are the published descriptive top-K (K in {1000, 2000, 5000}); a source HVG set is its top-2000 measured genes; a source DEG set is padj < 0.05 on the winning contrast.",
    "rank": "Within-source only. Measured genes are ranked 1..n_measured by descending score with gene_index as tie-break; unmeasured genes get n_measured + 1 and rank_norm = 1.0. Ranks are never compared across sources as raw effect sizes."
  },
